{"core": "Compassion feels what another feels and moves toward them. In Faith, it works on the held ground — the part that stays suspended in uncertainty, neither acting nor retreating, just waiting. Overdone, the feeling floods the suspension: someone else's weight pours in and fills the space the waiting needed. The ground gives way before the waiting is done.", "sheetLine": "Someone else's weight filled the suspension; the ground gave way too soon."}
